# intent spec

# AIDE HANDOFF

Cold-start protocol for agents reorienting on this project. This is a
snapshot of the current architectural intent and the anti-regression
invariants every build phase must hold. It is NOT historical commentary —
superseded design decisions are cut, not annotated.

---

## State summary (set 2026-04-28, mid-rework)

The previously landed brain-config + update-playbook rework (4→6 body
schema, 3→4 entry-point artifacts, optional `brainPath`, `<BRAIN_PATH>`
literal-sentinel placeholder design) was discovered to have a silent
failure-at-launch bug during smoke testing in `D:\Code\Me\aide-fresh`:
`<BRAIN_PATH>` propagated byte-for-byte into both `brain.aide` and
`.mcp.json`, the drift detector returned `ok` because the bytes agreed,
the orchestrator never routed to `/aide:brain config`, and the brain MCP
server failed silently at launch.

A SECOND rework is mid-pipeline to fix this structurally. The fix removes
the literal-sentinel design entirely and replaces it with YAML null as
the structural unwired-slot signal. The pipeline progress:

- **Stage 1 (frontmatter)** complete. Root `.aide/intent.aide` and 5
  module specs rewritten. Carve-out cleanup landed (legacy `obsidian`-key
  migration dropped from root + cli/sync). All approved.
- **Stage 3 (body synthesis)** complete. 7 specs body-refreshed (root + 6
  modules). All `aide_validate` clean. tools/brain duplicated stale body
  half deleted as part of cleanup.
- **Stage 4 (plan)** mostly complete. 5 plans written. 4 are ready to
  proceed. **1 needs revision** (`provisionBrain` — see below).
- **Stage 5 (build)** has NOT started.

The pipeline paused at Stage 4 review when the provisionBrain plan was
found to violate a load-bearing root-spec invariant.

---

## The architectural intent (what the specs say after the rewrite)

The brain layer is governed by the decisions below. Numbering matches the
prior handoff where invariants carry through; new decisions added at the
end.

1. **`brain.aide` lives at `.aide/config/brain.aide`.** The `.aide/config/`
   directory is user-owned: scaffolded once at `aide_init` if absent, never
   overwritten by `aide_init` or `aide_upgrade` after that. The directory path
   itself is the ownership signal — install/upgrade tooling reads it, no
   per-file allowlist.

2. **The default scaffolded launcher is `@bitbonsai/mcpvault`.** The bundled
   `obsidianBrainAideTemplate()` helper (NO `brainPath` parameter — see #11
   below) emits `cmd /c npx @bitbonsai/mcpvault <bare-yaml-null-at-args[3]>`.
   For Obsidian specifically, `args[3]` is YAML null until the user fills it
   via `/aide:brain config`. Other integrations would name a different index
   in their own bundled template.

3. **Frontmatter schema = exactly two top-level fields:** `name` (a
   human-readable label the package never branches on) and `mcpServerConfig`
   (`command` + `args` that sync writes verbatim into `.mcp.json` under
   `mcpServers["brain"]`).

4. **Body schema = exactly six marker-bounded sections, fixed order.**
   Twelve markers total, six pairs:
   - `<!-- aide-orientation-start -->` / `<!-- aide-orientation-end -->`
   - `<!-- aide-config-start -->` / `<!-- aide-config-end -->`
   - `<!-- aide-playbook-index-start -->` / `<!-- aide-playbook-index-end -->`
   - `<!-- aide-study-playbook-start -->` / `<!-- aide-study-playbook-end -->`
   - `<!-- aide-update-playbook-start -->` / `<!-- aide-update-playbook-end -->`
   - `<!-- aide-research-index-start -->` / `<!-- aide-research-index-end -->`

   Marker tokens are lowercase, case-sensitive, byte-exact form. Field names on
   the parsed result are camelCase: `orientation`, `config`, `playbookIndex`,
   `studyPlaybook`, `updatePlaybook`, `researchIndex`.

5. **Two structural categories of body section, enforced by per-consumer
   ownership at code level:**
   - **Live (read by `aide_brain` at runtime):** `orientation` (agent's
     runtime briefing), `config` (integration-specific wiring flow consumed
     by `/aide:brain config`).
   - **Install-time seeds:** `playbookIndex` → `coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md`,
     `studyPlaybook` → `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`,
     `updatePlaybook` → `coding-playbook/update-playbook.md`,
     `researchIndex` → `research/research.md`.

   Cross-section reads across this boundary are forbidden.

6. **`aide_brain({ kind?: "orientation" | "config" })`.** Closed two-value
   vocabulary, default `"orientation"`. Response shape `{ status, instructions }`
   only. Seed-section `kind` values are forbidden.

7. **`parseBrainAide` ok-variant is FLATTENED.** `name` and `mcpServerConfig`
   are siblings of the six body fields directly on `result`. `mcpServerConfig.args`
   is now typed `(string | null)[]` — see #20 below.

8. **Entry-point artifact bytes flow from `brain.aide` body sections, never
   from inline TypeScript constants.**

9. **The framework's brain contract = exactly four required entry-point
   artifacts:** `coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md`,
   `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`, `coding-playbook/update-playbook.md`,
   `research/research.md`. **NEW (post-rework):** these are seeded by the
   integration's `config` body section prose, NOT by `provisionBrain` —
   provisionBrain shrinks to brain.aide-scaffold + MCP-entry-plan only
   (see #21 below).

10. **Boot reporter brain status states = four:** `ok`, `no-brain-aide`,
    `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`. Closed vocabulary. Null-armed args collapse
    semantically into `no-mcp-entry` (see #22 below).

11. **`provisionBrain` accepts NO `brainPath` parameter at any layer.** No
    `brainPath` on the orchestrator signature, on any per-step builder, or
    on the bundled template helper. The bundled template emits YAML null at
    the path slot unconditionally.

12. **`cli/init` is argument-less and brain-agnostic.** It writes ZERO brain
    surfaces during install: no `brain.aide`, no `.mcp.json` brain entry, no
    `provisionBrain` call, no brain root directory creation, no
    backend-specific user prompts. It accepts no `--brain-path`,
    `--vault-path`, `--brain-root`, or any other brain-shaped flag in its
    current shape. Brain wiring is fully delegated to `/aide:brain config`
    on the first `/aide` run after install. The terminal warning routes the
    user there explicitly. Future `npx aidemd-mcp init --brain <integration>`
    is a forward-compatible extension that selects WHICH bundled template
    scaffolds on first config — but it must never collect backend-specific
    values at install time.

13. **Removed frontmatter fields:** `connector`, `rootPath`, `entryFile`,
    `tools`. The parser actively rejects these.

14. **No code path branches on `name`.** It's a label.

15. **No introspection of `mcpServerConfig.args` for any purpose.** This is a
    LOAD-BEARING invariant strengthened by the rework. See #23.

16. **Boot reporter brain status states = four:** `ok`, `no-brain-aide`,
    `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`.

17. **`${...}` interpolation of frontmatter values into `mcpServerConfig.args`
    is supported** for advanced users. The default scaffold does NOT exercise
    this surface. Substitution lives ONLY in `mcpServerConfig.args` at
    install/sync time — NEVER in any of the six body sections at any time.

18. **The MCP server never silently rewrites `.mcp.json`.** Sync is the only
    mutation surface for `mcpServers.brain`.

19. **Storage-agnostic vocabulary across every surface this package authors.**
    The forbidden-token list — `vault`, `obsidian`, `note` (used as a synonym
    for "file"), `wikilink`, `hub note`, and `hub` — must not appear in any
    user-facing prose surface NOR in code identifiers, comments, or string
    constants project-wide.

    **Three explicit carve-outs (was four pre-rework — legacy `obsidian` MCP
    key migration carve-out was dropped because legacy migration was dropped
    entirely):**
    - The `obsidianBrainAideTemplate` helper folder/function name (describes
      bundled template content, not a dispatch axis).
    - The `.obsidian` directory heuristic comment in `brainRootExists` (an
      honestly-labeled implementation detail).
    - **The body section bytes of the bundled `obsidianBrainAideTemplate`**
      across all six sections.

20. **`mcpServerConfig.args` is typed `(string | null)[]`.** Every element is
    a fully-formed string OR YAML null (a bare `-` with no scalar after,
    parses to JS `null`). Null at any index is the explicit, structural,
    unwired-slot signal. NO literal-string sentinel — `<BRAIN_PATH>`,
    `<API_TOKEN>`, `__UNWIRED__`, magic UUIDs, ANY in-band string the package
    recognizes as "fill me in" — is part of the design at any layer. The
    `<BRAIN_PATH>` design produced the byte-for-byte-agreement-passes-drift-check
    silent-failure bug; this rework deletes that class of failure.

21. **`provisionBrain` shrinks to a TWO-step pipeline (NOT seven):** brain
    config scaffold (writes `brain.aide` from bundled template, with YAML
    null at unwired slots) + MCP entry plan. **The four entry-point
    artifacts are seeded by the integration's `config` body section prose,
    NOT by provisionBrain.** This is the load-bearing fix for the
    PATH_SLOT_INDEX issue (see "Where this cycle stopped" below). The prose
    has access to the brain's MCP write tools (e.g. `mcp__brain__write_note`
    for Obsidian) and reads the seed-section bytes from `brain.aide` via
    `parseBrainAide`'s typed keys (`playbookIndex`, `studyPlaybook`,
    `updatePlaybook`, `researchIndex`), then writes each artifact at paths
    the integration's prose names. Slot-semantics, file-path, and
    write-tool-name knowledge ALL live in prose; provisionBrain becomes
    backend-blind.

22. **`buildBrainState` maps null entries in `mcpServerConfig.args` to
    `no-mcp-entry` immediately.** Detection is structural (JS `=== null`
    against parsed YAML), NOT pattern-matching string sentinels. The
    null-args check runs BEFORE the byte-for-byte drift comparison — this
    ordering is load-bearing because matching nulls on both sides of the
    drift check would otherwise pass through as `ok` (the original bug).
    Closed four-state vocabulary; no fifth state for null-armed configs.

23. **`cli/sync` refuses null-bearing args at the boundary.** If any element
    of `mcpServerConfig.args` is null at sync time, sync exits non-zero,
    names the offending index(es) in stderr, and routes the user to
    `/aide:brain config`. Sync is precondition-not-transformation: NO
    coercion to empty string, NO dropping null entries, NO substituting
    placeholders.

24. **`/aide:brain config` Mode 2 router calls `aide_init({ category: "brain" })`
    UNCONDITIONALLY** at the top of every invocation — not gated on
    `aide_info.brain.status`, not skipped when `brain.aide` already exists.
    The unconditional call enables missing-file recovery for the
    brain.aide artifact specifically; entry-point artifact recovery now
    happens via the integration prose's presence-check + re-seed loop after
    sync (see #21).

25. **Per-integration ownership of arg-index slot semantics.** The meaning
    of each slot in `mcpServerConfig.args` — which index is a path, which
    is a token, which is a connection URI — is documented EXCLUSIVELY
    inside that integration's `config` body section in its bundled
    `brain.aide` template. The bundled Obsidian default names `args[3]` as
    the absolute path to the user's brain root; future Mem0 / API-token
    integrations would name their own indexes in their own templates.
    The shipped code NEVER hardcodes a slot index, never has a
    `PATH_SLOT_INDEX` constant, never has a registry of slot meanings,
    never has a per-index validation table, never has an `argSlots`
    frontmatter field. Slot semantics live in user-owned prose, full
    stop.

26. **Legacy `mcpServers.obsidian` migration is dropped entirely.** Pre-rework
    hosts with the legacy key keep it as user data, untouched by this
    package. No code path reads, writes, removes, or detects the legacy
    key. The corresponding storage-agnostic-vocabulary carve-out was
    removed as vestigial (see #19).

27. **Strict-failure migration for body schema and frontmatter shape changes.**
    Pre-rework files fail closed as `malformed-body` or
    `malformed-frontmatter`. Users hand-edit. No `aide_upgrade` carve-out
    auto-migrates. No transitional read path. No auto-rename of retired
    markers. No auto-injection of missing pairs. No coercion of literal
    sentinels back to null.

28. **Shipped pipeline command surfaces are thin routers/pointers.**
    `.claude/commands/aide/brain.md` Mode 2 is now a 5-step router:
    `aide_info` → `aide_init({ category: "brain" })` UNCONDITIONALLY →
    `aide_brain({ kind: "config" })` → execute returned prose verbatim →
    STOP. The shipped command takes `$ARGUMENTS` opaquely and forwards it
    to the integration prose. **Note: the prior version had this call
    CONDITIONAL on `brain.status === "no-brain-aide"`. The build phase
    must flip this conditional to unconditional.**

29. **The AIDE pipeline is for code only.** `.claude/agents/`,
    `.claude/commands/`, `.claude/skills/` are never pipelined. Direct
    edits only. Per-command `.aide` specs are an anti-pattern.
    `.aide/docs/`, `.aide/intent.aide`, and `.aide/config/brain.aide` ARE
    pipeline-appropriate when their updates ride alongside a code
    amendment.

---

## Anti-regression invariants future build phases must hold

These are the hard rules from `.aide/intent.aide` outcomes.undesired plus
permanent additions from prior cycles. Many overlap with the architectural
intent above; they are listed here as imperatives the build agent must check
at every step.

- **Body schema is marker-bounded, not heading-bounded.**
- **No tolerant matching of marker variants.** Uppercase, mixed-case,
  stray-whitespace, missing-`aide-`-prefix variants are ALL rejected as
  malformed.
- **No transitional read path for pre-rework files.** Strict failure.
- **Field-name regression class.** No `Hub` suffix. The safe-list is exactly
  `orientation`, `config`, `playbookIndex`, `studyPlaybook`, `updatePlaybook`,
  `researchIndex`.
- **No retired-vocabulary leakage.** `prose`, `playbook` (unsuffixed), and
  `research` (unsuffixed) MUST NOT appear as live typed-key names or
  recognized markers.
- **No forbidden-token leakage** in code identifiers, JSDoc, parameter names,
  function names, or string constants outside the three explicit carve-outs
  in #19.
- **No code path branches on `name`.**
- **No introspection of `mcpServerConfig.args` for any purpose.** This now
  includes: no `PATH_SLOT_INDEX` constant, no `args[N]` switch, no
  matcher recognizing token-shaped strings at any index, no `argSlots`
  frontmatter field, no `resolveBrainRoot`-style helper that reads args[N]
  to extract a path. **The architect's proposed `PATH_SLOT_INDEX = 3` in
  `provisionBrain` is forbidden.**
- **No silent acceptance of deprecated frontmatter fields.**
- **No literal-string sentinel** anywhere in the unwired-slot design —
  `<BRAIN_PATH>`, `<API_TOKEN>`, `<VAULT_ROOT>`, `__UNWIRED__`, magic UUIDs,
  or any other in-band string the package recognizes. YAML null is the
  unwired-slot signal.
- **No coercion of null `mcpServerConfig.args` entries** to empty string,
  dropped entry, substituted placeholder, or any other transformation at
  any layer (parser, sync, buildBrainState, provisionBrain).
- **No fifth boot-reporter status state** for null-armed args. Null
  collapses into `no-mcp-entry`.
- **No conditional `aide_init({ category: "brain" })`** in `/aide:brain
  config`'s router. Unconditional call is what enables missing-file
  self-heal.
- **No `cli/init` brain-shaped flag** in the current shape (`--brain-path`,
  `--vault-path`, `--brain-root`, `--brain-token`, `--brain-url`,
  `--brain-name`).
- **No `cli/init` writing any brain surface** at install time — no
  `brain.aide`, no `.mcp.json` brain entry, no provisionBrain call, no
  brain root directory creation, no backend-specific user prompts.
- **No `provisionBrain` parameter named `brainPath`** at any layer
  (orchestrator, step builders, template helper).
- **No legacy `mcpServers.obsidian` migration code** anywhere in the
  package.
- **No silent `.mcp.json` mutation.** Sync is the only mutation surface
  AND requires deliberate user invocation.
- **No overwrite of files under `.aide/config/`** on subsequent
  `aide_init` / `aide_upgrade` runs.
- **No code-driven seeding of entry-point artifacts.** After the rework,
  entry-point artifacts (the four required ones in #9) are seeded by the
  integration's `config` body section prose, not by `provisionBrain` or
  any other shipped code path. The bytes flow from brain.aide seed sections
  via `parseBrainAide`; the writes happen via the brain's own MCP write
  tools at paths the prose names.
- **No backend-driver dispatch, no connector registry, no matcher-by-shape.**
- **No reading another consumer's owned body section.**
- **No `aide_brain` `kind` value exposing any install-time seed section.**
- **No shipped pipeline command file documenting integration-specific
  argument shape.** `<absolute-path>`, `<api-token>`, etc. live in the
  integration's `config` body section, not in
  `.claude/commands/aide/brain.md`.
- **No hardcoded sync invocation in any skill or command prompt.**
- **No re-call of `aide_info` (or any boot state read) after sync completes
  in the same session.**
- **`aide_info`'s outdated flag is not actionable in this repo.** This
  package IS the canonical source for every artifact under
  `.claude/agents/`, `.claude/commands/`, `.claude/skills/`, and
  `.aide/docs/`. Ignore the outdated array when working in this repo.

