  possibly the root `.aide/intent.aide` outcome about "the install service
  has scaffolded an entry-point artifact into the brain."

- **Whether `tools/brain/.aide`'s body Good examples need updating** — the
  example `config` body section there shows the old flow (just fill the
  null slot, sync, restart). Under the new contract, the prose ALSO seeds
  entry-point artifacts. Worth a review during the Stage 1/3 amendment
  pass.

- **Whether `.aide/handoff.aide` (this file) should itself be pipelined.**
  It's project-surface scoped and describes architectural intent; it could
  be a candidate. Currently it's hand-written between major reworks.

- **Whether the cli/init plan's Decision 4 wording fix needs a full Stage 4
  amendment or can be a direct edit.** Plan files are written by the
  architect; per the orchestrator delegation rule, the orchestrator
  shouldn't edit plans directly. But the wording fix is one sentence in
  the Decisions section.

